### 4.1 Deployment (Louis runs or approves each)

1. `npx wrangler login`, then `npx wrangler d1 create blacklist`; put the `database_id` in `wrangler.jsonc`; `npm run db:migrate:remote`; `npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`; `npm run deploy`. The key's Console organisation needs web search enabled (it is unless an admin disabled it) and a monthly spend limit. Each run is capped at 10 searches ($10 per 1,000) plus tokens.
2. In Zero Trust, add Microsoft Entra ID as an identity provider (login method). This needs an Entra app registration with redirect URI `https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com/cdn-cgi/access/callback`; group-based policies need admin consent.
3. Workers & Pages → blacklist → Access → Protect this Worker behind Access → All traffic. Policy: the SOC Entra group (or the Chorus email domain), with Entra ID as the only login method. Copy the team domain and the application AUD tag into `vars`, then `npm run deploy`.
4. First research run: set the cron to a daily time about 10 minutes ahead (keep it daily, because sub-hourly crons get only 30 s of CPU), deploy, confirm, restore `0 6 * * *` and deploy again.

### 4.2 Production acceptance (from the handover)

- A signed-out browser is sent to Entra sign-in. After sign-in, the profile shows the Chorus email, which proves the JWT reaches the Worker through the assets router. If every API call returns 401, stop and report.
- Two analysts on two accounts see each other's marks within 60 s with the correct name. An edit from a stale tab gets the 409 toast and reloads.
- Refresh intelligence shows `N new reports. X/5 sources refreshed.`; Sources & updates shows per-source health; a failed source keeps its earlier items.
- After the first research run: the status line is ok; at least one new or enriched briefing has working source links, publication and collection dates and its caveat; an enriched item keeps any existing Actioned mark.
- KQL copies, is labelled UNTESTED and shows its prerequisites.
- The seven-day boundary and concurrent-edit rejection are covered by `actioned.test.ts`. Report them as test-verified, not as observed in production.

